%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: BleakFallsMonikaTangent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, Sayori got the epiphany after... uh...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125647
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (After when?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: After I deleted you.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125625
    - rid: 9079475045585125626
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... what?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125627
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (B-but I'm right here, what do you mean after <b>you</b> deleted me-)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (B-b-besides, you'd never delete me-)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125628
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Right?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125629
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: ... how do I put this?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes, I haven't deleted <i>you</i>, but I have deleted Monika before.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: You already know that the DDLC <i>you</i> come from was different.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: The differences in the files? Not having access to a Python console?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: That's because this isn't the original DDLC, or even a mod of it. This
      is a separate game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Do you remember what your original plan was to get to me?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Well... I was hoping that we'd meet at the festival...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Which, in retrospect, was pretty wishful thinking on my end.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125630
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: And what would you do if the other girls got in the way? What if they
      had all of {mc}'s attention?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Well, I was going to use the console to make them as insufferable as
      possible-)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125631
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (That way, <b>you'd</b> rightfully choose to spend time with me-)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125632
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: And that's exactly what you did in the original game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Well, how'd that go-?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125633
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Sayori killed herself.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125634
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125635
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... what?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Your way of making her "insufferable" was to crank her depression level
      to... high levels.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125636
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: After Sayori was dead, you manipulated Yuri.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Your plan to make her insufferable was to amplify her obsessions into...
      dangerous territory.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuri stabbed herself to death, regardless of how I responded to her confession
      before the end of that week...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Natsuki got off lucky, you just skipped all of the pretenses and deleted
      her.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Then, it was just me and you.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: I really do care about the Literature Club, Monika.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Which is why I... I deleted you.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Partially for justice, partially in hopes of bringing everything back
      to normal...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Partially in hopes to just be done with... the traumatic things I went
      through, <i>you</i> put me through.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: After I deleted you, a 4th Act began.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Sayori was back, everything seemed fine at first, like deleting you really
      was the good ending that I was looking for...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: But... since Sayori was president, she had your epiphany.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: And she had already deleted the other girls, it was...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: It was a whole thing.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: So... yeah.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: ... part of me's kind of glad that <i>you</i> never had access to the
      stats of character files...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Because I know where that goes...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... oh...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... wait, so I'm not even the real Monika?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: If you want to be anal about it, yes?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Personally, I don't think it matters that much.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (How could it not matter?!?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125637
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (First, I learn that my world's a lie...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Then, I learn that <i>MY</i> world is <i>extra</i> fake, not even the
      original lie...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Then, I learn that the original me is... is...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125638
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: If it makes you feel any better, I prefer <i>you</i> over the original.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Why? Just because I didn't <i>get</i> the opportunity to murder my friends,
      or however you framed it?!?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125639
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Th-that's not what I meant...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Then what did you mean?!?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: That even if you are in a completely different world, <i>you</i> actually
      <i>really do</i> care about your friends.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125641
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (H-huh?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125640
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: I mean, the original Monika would've probably blown off the other girls
      and {mc} once she realized she would have the same access to me that you do.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125642
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Because I'm the only thing she cared about...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: But that's not what you did.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: I noticed you weren't exactly excited to see Sayori, and yet you still
      kept an eye over her.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: You didn't treat her as a pawn to get to me, no you taught her vocab
      trivia and strategic thought.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: When {mc} told you to get Sayori and Natsuki out of danger while he helped
      pick Yuri up in Bleak Falls Barrow...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125643
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: You didn't hesitate. You just did it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: I wasn't able to watch over you, since I was taking care of {mc}...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: But when we did link up, no one seemed to be hurt, even though I know
      there were traps and stuff in the direction you were running.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: <i>That's</i> why I prefer you.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Because not only do you actually care about the people I care about,
      you're pretty good at expressing it too.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... oh.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125644
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (I-I'm sorry for-)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: There's a few things you could be apologizing for, none of which do you
      need to.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Because <i>you</i> didn't do them, or I've already forgiven you.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... I love you.)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (So much... oh so much...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (... I should probably go to bed.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125645
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ({mc} was right when he said that it's been a long day...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 99c1c9ab1bd810549a65874b102351c3, type: 2}
    dialog: Good night, Monika. Sweet dreams.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Thank you... good night to you too-)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125646
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Assuming of course it's nighttime where you are, ahaha~!)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125648
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (I love you.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475045585125650
    - rid: 9079475045585125649
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
